---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const pnpmInstall = `# Install client packages for React
pnpm add @copypatch/react @copypatch/core

# For Next.js App Router (SSR) support:
pnpm add @copypatch/next

# For standalone server & CLI:
pnpm add @copypatch/server`;

const npmInstall = `# Install client packages with npm
npm install @copypatch/react @copypatch/core

# For Next.js App Router:
npm install @copypatch/next

# For standalone server:
npm install @copypatch/server`;

const initDb = `# Initialize SQLite database and set administrative passphrase
npx copypatch init --db ./copypatch.sqlite`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Installation"
  description="How to install and set up CopyPatch in your React, Vite, or Next.js project."
>
  <h1>Installation & Setup</h1>

  <p>
    CopyPatch consists of lightweight modular packages published under the <code>@copypatch</code> npm namespace.
  </p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Node.js:</strong> <code>&gt;= 20.0.0</code></li>
    <li><strong>React:</strong> <code>&gt;= 18.0.0</code> or <code>19.x</code></li>
    <li><strong>Package Manager:</strong> <code>pnpm</code> (recommended), <code>npm</code>, or <code>yarn</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Package Overview</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Package</th>
        <th>Description</th>
        <th>Target Environment</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>@copypatch/react</code></td>
        <td>Client provider, <code>EditableText</code>, and hooks</td>
        <td>React / Vite / Next.js Client</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>@copypatch/core</code></td>
        <td>Shared types, constants, and validation</td>
        <td>Universal</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>@copypatch/next</code></td>
        <td>Next.js App Router RSC snapshot pre-rendering</td>
        <td>Next.js Server & Client</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>@copypatch/server</code></td>
        <td>Hono API server, SQLite persistence, and CLI</td>
        <td>Node.js Server</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>1. Install Dependencies</h2>

  <h3>Using pnpm</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={pnpmInstall} lang="bash" title="Terminal" />

  <h3>Using npm</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={npmInstall} lang="bash" title="Terminal" />

  <h2>2. Initialize SQLite Database</h2>
  <p>
    Use the built-in CLI to initialize your single-file SQLite database with automatic migrations and interactive passphrase configuration:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={initDb} lang="bash" title="Terminal" />

  <p>
    This command will prompt you for an editor passphrase (minimum 12 characters recommended), hash it using <strong>Argon2id</strong>, and create the SQLite database schema in <strong>WAL (Write-Ahead Logging)</strong> mode.
  </p>

  <h2>Next Step</h2>
  <p>
    Continue to the <a href="/docs/react">React & Vite Integration Guide</a> to wire CopyPatch into your user interface.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
